Use IOptionsMonitor to read updated data

[Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsMonitor1](xref:Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsMonitor1) is used to retrieve options and manage options notifications for TOptions instances.

The difference between [Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsMonitor1](xref:Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsMonitor1) and IOptionsSnapshot is that:

• [Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsMonitor1](xref:Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsMonitor1) is a singleton service that retrieves current option values at any time, which is especially useful in singleton dependencies.

• [Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsSnapshot1](xref:Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsSnapshot1) is a scoped service and provides a snapshot of the options at the time the IOptionsSnapshot<T> object is constructed. Options snapshots are designed for use with transient and scoped dependencies.

[Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsMonitorCache1](xref:Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsMonitorCache1) is used by [Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsMonitor1](xref:Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsMonitor1) to cache TOptions instances. [Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsMonitorCache1.TryRemove*?displayProperty=nameWithType](xref:Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsMonitorCache1.TryRemove*?displayProperty=nameWithType) invalidates options instances in the monitor so that the value is recomputed. Values can be manually introduced with [Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsMonitorCache1.TryAdd*?displayProperty=nameWithType](xref:Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsMonitorCache1.TryAdd*?displayProperty=nameWithType). The [Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsMonitorCache1.Clear*](xref:Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptionsMonitorCache1.Clear*) method is used when all named instances should be recreated on demand.

